system "UN:bul-Cyrl:Latn:1977" {

metadata {
  authority_id un
  id 1977
  language iso-639-2:bul
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name Romanization of Bulgarian geographical names (1977)
  url https://www.eki.ee/wgrs/res/res_3_10.htm
  creation_date 1977
  description {    The System of Transliteration and Transcription of Bulgarian Geographical Names into Roman letters,
    as shown in the annex below, be adopted as the international system for the romanization of Bulgarian geographical names.
  }

  notes {
    note "Diffed against the UN WGRS Report on the Current Status of UN Romanization\n Systems for Geographical Names, version 4.0 (February 2013)\n (eki.ee/wgrs/rom1_bg.htm; also unstats wgrr4bulgarian): the 1977 system\n (res. III/10, adopting the 1972 Council of Orthography system) is printed there\n as a comparison against the superseding 2009/2012 system; all 30 rows verified."

    note "Rows ю and я now render ju/ja per the 1977 system; the map previously\n carried yu/ya, the values of the superseding current system (2009 Transliteration\n Act, UN-approved 2012 X/7). Reissue note: the current system differs from 1977\n in zh/j/ts/ch/sh/sht/a/y/yu/ya; it is NOT encoded here."

    note "The full text of res. III/10 (eki.ee/wgrs/res/res_3_10.htm) is not in the\n reference library; the 1977 rows were verified against the UN WGRS 4.0\n comparison section, which lists every row in which the 1977 system differs\n from the current one. The -iya -> -ia word-final footnote of the current table\n is likewise not attested for the 1977 system and is not encoded."
  }
}

tests {
   "ю" ->  "ju"
   "я" ->  "ja"
   "Ю" ->  "Ju"
   "Я" ->  "Ja"
   "ь" ->  "j"
   "ъ" ->  "ǎ"
